From: KOReader <https://github.com/koreader/koreader-base>
Subject: [PATCH] willuslib/ansi: drop the Win32 fast path in avprintf()

`trim the fat` (#50) disabled the ANSI parsing machinery (`ansi_on`,
`ansi_buffer`, `ansi_parse`, `ansi_code`), but only guarded the POSIX side
of `avprintf()` with `#if 0`. The `#ifdef WIN32` fast path kept calling
`ansi_parse()`/`ansi_buffer`, so any Windows build fails to compile
(MinGW predefines `WIN32`):

    willuslib/ansi.c:330:25: error: 'ansi_buffer' undeclared (first use in this function)
    willuslib/ansi.c:58:13: warning: 'ansi_parse' used but never defined

As the ANSI parsing code is gone, so is the point of that path: always
fall through to `vfprintf()`.

--- a/willuslib/ansi.c
+++ b/willuslib/ansi.c
@@ -324,25 +324,7 @@ int avprintf(FILE *f,const char *fmt,va_list args)
     {
     int     status;
 
-#ifdef WIN32
-    if (wsys_win32_api())
-        {
-        status=vsprintf(ansi_buffer,fmt,args);
-        ansi_parse(f,ansi_buffer);
-        }
-    else
-#endif
-        {
-#if 0
-        if (!ansi_on)
-            {
-            status=vsprintf(ansi_buffer,fmt,args);
-            ansi_parse(f,ansi_buffer);
-            }
-        else
-#endif
-            status=vfprintf(f,fmt,args);
-        }
+    status=vfprintf(f,fmt,args);
     return(status);
     }
 
